TITLE:: SPInspector
summary:: the panel of SPTree that says everything about one node: who made it, controls, busses, UGens
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/SPTree, Classes/SPScope, Classes/ServerPanel, Classes/SynthDesc

DESCRIPTION::
Beside nodes it shows a strong::bus:: (click one in the tree's busses view, or in a signal path): its level, what looks wrong with it, the synths that write it and those that read it in the order they run, each a button to that node, and strong::path::, strong::scope::, strong::freq::, strong::listen::, strong::watch::. And a strong::buffer::: its file and the synths that read it. For a synth it adds what looks wrong with it, the buffers its controls name, strong::path:: (where its sound goes), strong::freq:: and strong::listen:: on the bus it writes, and a strong::w:: beside each control to keep its value in view under the tree.

The panel at the right of link::Classes/SPTree::. It is made by the tree; click a node there, running or under strong::recent::, and it shows:

list::
## what it is and who made it, from link::Classes/SPTree#*describers:: (an Ndef, an orbit's global effect, a synth of one SuperDirt event, and whatever a system of yours says - SuperDirtGUI names its faders, inserts, tracks, returns and the content file of an event's synth);
## the groups above it, by name;
## whether it runs or is paused, and how long it has been seen. Paused is known from the server's notifications (code::/n_off::, code::/n_on::), so only since the window opened;
## its controls, with values and defaults. Type a value and return to set it (code::/n_set:: by index); a control mapped to a bus says which in its tooltip; an array control is one row;
## the busses it reads and writes, with names from link::Classes/SPTree#*busNamers::, read from its SynthDef's code::In::, code::InFeedback::, code::Out:: and code::ReplaceOut:: UGens and the controls that feed them;
## the UGens inside it.
::

Its buttons: strong::trace:: (code::/n_trace::: every UGen's inputs and outputs, once, into the post window), strong::pause:: / strong::run::, strong::free:: (click twice), strong::scope out:: (the bus it writes in link::Classes/SPScope:: - the whole bus, not only this synth's part), strong::source:: (the file a describer named), strong::copy:: (a line of code that reaches it, onto the clipboard and into the post window), strong::post:: (all of it as text), and a describer's own actions. For a group: strong::dump:: (code::/g_dumpTree::), pause, free (everything inside), copy, post, and the defs it holds.

What the SynthDef says - defaults, busses, UGens - needs its link::Classes/SynthDesc:: in this sclang, which every def made with code::.add:: has. The selected synth's values are asked for with code::/s_getn:: through it; without one, from its group's tree.

The class methods are the inspector's knowledge, usable on their own:

code::
s.boot;
SPTree(s);
SPInspector.textOf(SPTree(s).recordOf(s.defaultGroup.nodeID), s).postln;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Made by link::Classes/SPTree::.
ARGUMENT:: tree
The SPTree it belongs to.

METHOD:: textOf
Everything about a node, as text: what code::post:: writes.
ARGUMENT:: record
link::Classes/SPTree#-recordOf::'s answer.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/String::

METHOD:: controlRows
A synth's controls as rows: Events with code::label::, code::index::, code::value:: and code::default::, or code::values:: and code::array: true:: for an array control.
ARGUMENT:: record
A record with code::def:: and code::controls::.

METHOD:: ioRows
The busses a synth reads and writes: Events with code::dir:: (code::\in:: or code::\out::), code::type::, code::rate::, code::channels::, code::bus:: (nil when worked out in the graph or mapped), code::via:: (the control that sets it) and code::name::.
ARGUMENT:: record
A record with code::def:: and code::controls::.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.

METHOD:: ugenSummary
code::"7 UGens: BinaryOpUGen ×4, SinOsc ×2, Out"::, or nil without the def.
ARGUMENT:: desc
A link::Classes/SynthDesc::.

METHOD:: descOf
The SynthDesc of a def in code::SynthDescLib.global::, or nil.
ARGUMENT:: def
A SynthDef's name.

METHOD:: numControls
How many control values a SynthDesc's synth has.
ARGUMENT:: desc
A link::Classes/SynthDesc::.

METHOD:: namedValues
Values by index as code::[name or index, value]:: pairs, the way code::/g_queryTree:: lists them.
ARGUMENT:: desc
A link::Classes/SynthDesc::.
ARGUMENT:: values
The values, by index.

METHOD:: codeOf
A line of code that reaches the node: code::Synth.basicNew:: or code::Group.basicNew::.
ARGUMENT:: record
A record.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.

METHOD:: stateOf
code::"running, seen for 12.0 s"::, code::"paused for 3.1 s"::, code::"gone 2.0 s ago, seen for 150 ms"::.
ARGUMENT:: record
A record.
ARGUMENT:: now
The time to measure from; code::Main.elapsedTime:: when nil.

METHOD:: ioText
One of link::#*ioRows:: in words.
ARGUMENT:: r
A row.

METHOD:: mappedText
A mapped control's value (code::c12::, code::a12::) in words, or nil for a plain value.
ARGUMENT:: v
The value.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.

METHOD:: descFinders
A link::Classes/List:: of functions code::{ |defName| }:: answering a link::Classes/SynthDesc:: or nil, asked when the SynthDescLib does not have a def. Built in: JITLib - an Ndef's or a ProxySpace's proxy keeps the SynthDef of each of its synths, so their controls, busses and UGens are known too.

METHOD:: valueString
A value as the panel writes it.
ARGUMENT:: v
A number, Symbol or String.

METHOD:: duration
Seconds in words: code::"150 ms"::, code::"2.0 s"::, code::"3 min 5s"::.
ARGUMENT:: t
Seconds.

METHOD:: serverCode
What to write for a server in code: code::s:: for the default one.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.

METHOD:: copy
Onto the clipboard (pbcopy, clip or xclip) and into the post window.
ARGUMENT:: str
The text.

METHOD:: openSource
Open a file: in the IDE when there is one, else with the system's program for it.
ARGUMENT:: path
The file.

METHOD:: width
The panel's width in pixels.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: show
Show a record (nil for nothing). Built again when another node is shown, only the values otherwise.
ARGUMENT:: argRecord
link::Classes/SPTree#-recordOf::'s answer.

METHOD:: tree
The link::Classes/SPTree:: it belongs to.

METHOD:: view
Its link::Classes/ScrollView::.

METHOD:: server
The tree's server.

METHOD:: font
A font of the panel.
ARGUMENT:: size
Points.
ARGUMENT:: bold
Bold or not.

METHOD:: levels
The levels have moved: what shows one is written again, four times a second at most. link::Classes/SPTree:: calls it.
